{id:"Home.highestMarketSeller",defaultMessage:"Highest market seller {month}"},PBn={id:"Home.highestResearchInvestment",defaultMessage:"Highest research investment"},TBn={id:"Home.topValueCreators",defaultMessage:"Top value creators (EVA) {month}"},OBn={id:"Home.beATycoon",defaultMessage:"Be a tycoon"},IBn={id:"Home.buildYourOwn",defaultMessage:"Build your own company from the ground up. Find and exploit gaps in the market and compete against other players."},MBn={id:"Home.freeToPlay",defaultMessage:"Free to play"},RBn={id:"Home.freeGainSkills",defaultMessage:"Simcompanies is free to play for everyone! Gain valuable business skills for free :)"},NBn={id:"Home.economySimulation",defaultMessage:"Economy simulation"},DBn={id:"Home.haveYouEverWondered",defaultMessage:"Have you ever wondered what it would be like to build your own company, to be a tycoon?"},LBn={id:"Home.measureYourSkills",defaultMessage:"Do you want to measure your skills against other players in a virtual economy? Do you want to own a production, retail or research company which pays out the best? It all depends on the current conditions in the virtual economy and how skillful you are in spotting business opportunities. Sim Companies is an extremely versatile browser game that allows you to experiment with various resources and test your skills against other players in the game. Sim Companies is a business simulation strategy game aimed at giving you the fun and experience of managing a company using real world economic principles. The goal of the game is to create a profitable and competitive business. Each player receives a starting capital and few assets. Players' day-to-day tasks consist of managing the resource supply chain, from production to selling in retail, procuring business partners, ensuring financing, etc. For players to prosper, they would have to be able to read market conditions and take some trading shortcuts here and there, maybe buy their input resources on market cheaper than if they produced them or sell them on the market with higher profit than in the retail. When should players invest into research? We thought about what makes company management fun and what makes it tedious. Sim companies' philosophy is to let you take the interesting decisions while building your own business without having to fill in tons of extra settings. We do not want to simulate the real world with all its law and other restrictions, but rather give players the freedom to make decisions that can impact their company finances and value."},jBn={id:"Home.gainBusinessSkills",defaultMessage:"Gain business skills"},FBn={id:"Home.peoplePlaying",defaultMessage:"People playing Sim Companies are gaining knowledge and improving their skills in teamwork, business operations, leadership, and business development. Learning by active involvement is an established method that guarantees long term skill retention. The game rewards players with achievement badges. Companies are rewarded for employing people, building infrastructure, making profits off the market and other activities. This gratification ensures positive feedback when the right decisions are taken and provides good and viable short term goals when starting your business from scratch. This is similar to government incentives for small businesses that you would expect in the real world. Sim Companies gets its edge from an advanced economic model that simulates retail industry response to the supply and pricing that virtual companies provide. The players have control over quantity and price when offering goods in their stores. Retail parameters of all players are combined to simulate how fast the goods sold. Players can withdraw from selling for a period of time to temporarily increase the demand which would allow them to sell at higher rates later. There's no linear path to success, the decisions are good and bad based on current market and retail conditions. There's no sure strategy of winning and even if you found the right strategy, there are always ways to improve it. More importantly, if other players find your strategy; it will become less and less profitable, especially if everyone starts using it."},BBn={id:"Home.freeMarket",defaultMessage:"Free market simulation"},$Bn={id:"Home.coolThings",defaultMessage:"One of the incredibly realistic features you get to experience is the live, ever-changing, free market. Guess if the price of a certain resource will go up or down? Would you like to take a risk? Maybe you can trigger a certain price change yourself. Understanding the market dynamics is a very useful skill for someone to have. Players can, and the game too influences them to exchange resources among themselves. Players can also specialize in certain parts of the resource chain which yields the most profit. It is also challenging for the user to find the right business partners and negotiate prices. The (supplier-consumer) relationship is further supported by the Sim Companies concept of contracts where companies interested in or with long term relationships can exchange resources directly, saving on market fees."},UBn={id:"Home.simCompaniesBrowserGame",defaultMessage:"Sim Companies is a browser game with an amazing platform for strategic multiplayer games. Sim Companies is optimized to run smoothly on handheld devices, like phones or tablets. The game interface was designed for the phone platforms first. This gets us an amazing user experience on small devices as well as desktops. Sim Companies runs on all iOS and Android devices through a browser."},HBn={id:"Home.areYouATeacher",defaultMessage:"Are you a teacher?"},zBn={id:"Home.checkoutTeachers",defaultMessage:"Checkout how Sim Companies can be used in educational setting."},VBn={id:"Home.forSchools",defaultMessage:"For schools"},GBn={id:"Home.frequentlyAskedQuestions",defaultMessage:"Frequently Asked Questions"},qBn={id:"Home.youMightWantToPreffer",defaultMessage:"You might prefer this page in {language}"},WBn={id:"Home.anAdvancedProprietaryModel",defaultMessage:"An advanced, proprietary, {simulationModel} is used to deliver the best gaming experience. Form cartels, influence prices! There is no limits to what you can do."},qv={id:"Home.topRankStartedIn",defaultMessage:"Top in rank (started in {year})"},Vie={id:"Home.topRankResetIn",defaultMessage:"Top in rank (reset in {year})"},THt={id:"Home.topCertificateHunters",defaultMessage:"Top certificate hunters"},YBn={id:"Home.topEggCollectors",defaultMessage:"Top egg collectors"},ZBn={id:"Home.meetTheTeam",defaultMessage:"Meet the Sim Companies team"},KBn={id:"Home.aboutStory1",defaultMessage:"Sim Companies started as a hobby project in late 2015. I wanted to play a business simulation game, but I couldn't find one I liked. I had a working concept by the start of 2016, purchased the domain, and slowly added more and more features. I got a few friends to play with me, which helped me discover a lot of early bugs and helped shape the economy. They also pointed out that the graphics could use some improvement, so I hired freelancers to help me out in areas where I lacked the necessary skills."},XBn={id:"Home.aboutStory2",defaultMessage:"In September 2017, the game started landing high in the Google search results, and we started getting real traffic and the player base grew. It was like a switch had flipped. This was incredibly exciting, as all the work I put into the game now had more meaning. The fact that other people were enjoying something I created filled me with joy. I am incredibly lucky that what started as a hobby project of mine turned into something players want to support, allowing me to work on it full-time and build a dream team to help out."},QBn={id:"Home.aboutStorySignature",defaultMessage:"Patrik Beck"},JBn={id:"Home.teamMemberPatrikName",defaultMessage:"Patrik Beck"},e$n={id:"Home.teamMemberPatrikRole",defaultMessage:"Game design, Engineering, Operations"},t$n={id:"Home.teamMemberVaclavName",defaultMessage:"Václav Sobotka"},r$n={id:"Home.teamMemberVaclavRole",defaultMessage:"Game design, Engineering, Marketing"},n$n={id:"Home.teamMemberStanislavName",defaultMessage:"Stanislav Dudáš"},i$n={id:"Home.teamMemberStanislavRole",defaultMessage:"Graphics design, Marketing, Socials"},a$n={id:"Home.teamMemberTheCenterName",defaultMessage:"The Center"},o$n={id:"Home.teamMemberTheCenterRole",defaultMessage:"Support, Community Management"},s$n={id:"Home.linkedIn",defaultMessage:"LinkedIn"},l$n={id:"Home.teamMemberCompanyProfile",defaultMessage:"View {name}'s company profile"},c$n={id:"Home.simEnergyEmpireLogoAlt",defaultMessage:"Sim Energy Empire"},u$n={id:"Home.whyIsItFree",defaultMessage:"Why is it free?"},d$n={id:"Home.about3",defaultMessage:"We believe the best stuff in life is free! At the beginning, there was no point in charging anything — it was just Patrik and a few friends playing, and server costs were negligible."},p$n={id:"Home.about4",defaultMessage:"However, the game now depends on many third-party services that are only free when traffic is low. With our current player base, the server infrastructure needs to handle over 200 requests per second. It is not possible to keep Sim Companies running without some form of monetization. With that said, our intent is to keep Sim Companies free to play for everyone who does not want to spend money."},f$n={id:"Home.about5",defaultMessage:"Thank you for your support — it helps us maintain the servers, improve the game, and keep building new features."},g$n={id:"Home.thankPlayers",defaultMessage:"Thank you, players"},m$n={id:"Home.thankPlayersText",defaultMessage:"Above all, we want to thank you — the players. Your feedback, bug reports, guides, and day-to-day trading are what make the economy feel alive. Sim Companies would not exist without you."},h$n={id:"Home.articlesAndPress",defaultMessage:"Articles and press coverage"},v$n={id:"Home.pressStarterStory",defaultMessage:"StarterStory — how Patrik built Sim Companies"},y$n={id:"Home.pressLevelDo",defaultMessage:"LevelDo — interview with Patrik Beck"},b$n={id:"Home.pressGameIndustry",defaultMessage:"GameIndustry.com — when a business sim becomes an educational tool"},_$n={id:"Home.presskit",defaultMessage:"Anyone referring to Sim Companies on their website - you can use {presskit}."},w$n={id:"Home.thankModerators",defaultMessage:"Lastly, I want to thank our awesome {moderatingTeam}. Many of you point out our great community in your reviews. It's all thanks to our vigilant moderators who are there to help and keep chat rooms and guides organised."},S$n={id:"Home.moderatingTeam",defaultMessage:"moderating team"},x$n={id:"Home.whatsNext",defaultMessage:"What's next?"},E$n={id:"Home.whatsNextText",defaultMessage:"You send us a lot of ideas we would like to make a reality. Many of these suggestions would make the game even more exciting to play. We are working through them as fast as we can! Do you have a great idea as well? {link}"},C$n={id:"Home.findOutHowToSubmit",defaultMessage:"Find out how to submit your ideas."},k$n={id:"Home.becomeABusinessTycoon",defaultMessage:"Become{linebreak}a Business Tycoon"},A$n={id:"Home.buildYourOwnCompany2",defaultMessage:"Build your own company from the ground up."},P$n={id:"Home.jumbotronText",defaultMessage:"Simcompanies is free to play for everyone!{linebreak}Gain valuable business skills for free.{linebreak}An advanced, proprietary, {simulationModel} is used to{linebreak}deliver the best gaming experience."},T$n={id:"Home.switchLanguageTo",defaultMessage:"Switch language to {languageName}"},OHt={id:"Home.simEnergyEmpire",defaultMessage:"Sim Energy Empire"},IHt={id:"Home.simEnergyEmpireDescription",defaultMessage:"From the Sim Companies team: build power plants, connect cities, and compete in a live multiplayer energy market driven by weather, demand shifts, and rival companies."},MHt={id:"Home.playSimEnergyEmpire",defaultMessage:"Play Sim Energy Empire"},O$n={id:"Home.leaderboards",defaultMessage:"Leaderboards"}